WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:06.081
This video downloads one basin, 02070002,
North Branch Potomac,

00:00:06.081 --> 00:00:11.040
runs it for four years, and shows the flow
at its outlet.

00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:16.290
Open a terminal, go to the SWATrust
folder, and type ./swatrust.

00:00:16.490 --> 00:00:20.560
SWATrust prints the folder of its runs and
the address of its page.

00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:22.620
Open the address in your browser.

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:24.770
The page opens on Set-up.

00:00:24.970 --> 00:00:26.660
The list of models is empty.

00:00:27.161 --> 00:00:33.051
Under the map, type 02070002 in the box
Code or name.

00:00:33.251 --> 00:00:35.251
The page marks the row of the basin.

00:00:35.751 --> 00:00:38.201
Leave Basin alone, and click Download.

00:00:44.937 --> 00:00:53.327
The basin is in the list Models, with its
895 HRUs and its years, 1997 to 2025.

00:00:53.829 --> 00:00:56.829
On the map under the list, the basin is
drawn in yellow.

00:00:57.329 --> 00:00:59.158
To see the relief of the basin,

00:00:59.158 --> 00:01:03.699
with its streams and a red dot at its
outlet, click This basin above the map.

00:01:06.892 --> 00:01:09.712
In First year, type 2010 and press Enter.

00:01:11.378 --> 00:01:14.348
In Last year, type 2013 and press Enter.

00:01:14.848 --> 00:01:17.128
In Warm-up, type 1 and press Enter.

00:01:17.753 --> 00:01:20.773
The run now covers 4 years, the first as
warm-up.

00:01:20.973 --> 00:01:24.453
The warm-up year is simulated, but not
written to the tables.

00:01:24.954 --> 00:01:28.504
Leave Output tables as it is, and click
Continue to Run.

00:01:29.893 --> 00:01:31.263
The Run view opens.

00:01:31.463 --> 00:01:35.543
Checks before the run has one line for
each thing that SWATrust checked.

00:01:36.045 --> 00:01:37.225
Click Start the run.

00:01:39.881 --> 00:01:43.371
The run table shows the basin as Running,
and then as Finished.

00:01:49.162 --> 00:01:50.392
Click See the results.

00:01:55.069 --> 00:01:57.689
The Results view shows the run in three
columns.

00:01:58.189 --> 00:02:02.683
On the left, Output checks and Water
balance, average year sum the run up,

00:02:02.683 --> 00:02:07.419
and Output folders has the button Open
output folder for the basin of the run.

00:02:07.921 --> 00:02:11.320
In the middle, the basin is drawn as a
block on its relief,

00:02:11.320 --> 00:02:14.891
with each subbasin in the color of its
value on the day shown.

00:02:15.091 --> 00:02:20.277
Under it, a chart draws the daily flow at
the basin outlet in m³/s,

00:02:20.277 --> 00:02:25.231
from 2011, the first year after the
warm-up, to the end of 2013.

00:02:25.732 --> 00:02:28.209
On the right are the counts of the basin,

00:02:28.209 --> 00:02:31.712
its values on the day shown, and a table
of the subbasins.

00:02:32.213 --> 00:02:34.773
Read the table Water balance, average
year.

00:02:34.973 --> 00:02:37.812
It gives the parts of the water balance of
the

00:02:37.812 --> 00:02:40.713
land in mm and as a share of the
precipitation.

00:02:41.213 --> 00:02:42.053
Click Play.

00:02:44.685 --> 00:02:46.564
The date moves through the run,

00:02:46.564 --> 00:02:50.685
and the subbasins change color with the
value chosen under Color by.

00:02:51.193 --> 00:02:52.513
Click Pause to stop.

00:02:54.100 --> 00:02:56.360
Click a row of the table of subbasins.

00:02:57.452 --> 00:03:00.192
The chart now draws the flow from that
subbasin,

00:03:00.192 --> 00:03:02.362
and the right column gives its counts.

00:03:02.864 --> 00:03:04.754
Click Entire basin to go back.

00:03:06.451 --> 00:03:10.071
To stop SWATrust, press Ctrl-C in the
terminal window.
